                        "entry_id": "971cb22f-a528-37c8-8680-7b581dbd3502",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A small ape of the family Hylobatidae with long limbs, which they use to travel through rainforests by swinging from branch to branch."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9e694d4-776f-4651-bfaf-84da3f3b450b",
                                "sense_id": "9fe22bd5-6ed8-32e1-945a-e24c6860bc37",
                                "text": "'[…] Suppose that in years to come, when the Church's troubles seem to be over, there should come an apostate of my own trade, a false historian, with the mind of Cicero or Tacitus and the soul of an animal,' and he nodded towards the gibbon who fretted his golden chain and chattered for fruit."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
